# =====================================================================
# What stays out
# =====================================================================
# The question bank IS in this repo — it is AI-authored (400 CORE DEMO
# authoring agents, `provenance.generated_by: core-demo authoring agent`),
# not textbook material. Publishing it is the point: the whole project is
# an argument that AI-generated questions are unreliable until verified,
# and that argument is unfalsifiable without the corpus and the evidence.
#
# What still stays out is machine-local or regenerable:

# local config: absolute paths and machine-specific locations
config.yaml

# regenerable pipeline scratch (reports and state are rebuilt by the
# scripts; committing them just makes diffs noisy)
out/reports/
out/pack_diffs/
out/*.tmp

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.*
*.key

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
build/

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/

# Public repo: never commit textbook source material (Hanlon 4e text)
chapter_*_clean.txt
chapter_*.txt
textbook/
hanlon*
course_notes/
